# ---- the flat sources in /usr/src/cmd --------------------------------------
# One rule per entry, in the order `ls' gives them, each carrying the CFLAGS
# Admin/large decides and installing where Admin/dest routes.  What is above
# this line is not repeated here: those fifty-odd commands are the ones the
# disk needs to run, and they keep the rules that carry their evidence.
#
# NINE ARE COMPILED -O AND NOT Admin/large's -Od2, and it is the same deviation
# track, pstat and fstat above already carry: -Od2 reaches as as -d2, asmain.c
# :241 makes that the displacement size, and cc.c:262 hands dflag straight to
# as, so the object gets word displacements and ld answers `word displacement
# overflow' -- once per reference, hundreds of lines of it.  bc, deroff, find,
# logtty, netfsbug, passwdx, patch, settod and spline all overflow them, and
# 4014 joins them once ./patch turns its three gtty/stty calls into ioctls --
# the call is longer, and the object that fitted before does not.  The
# tape's own makefiles hit this too, in dc, numdate, ul and at, where the flag
# is written into the makefile and not taken from a variable this can set.
#
# Five of these need something the plain `cc -o x x.c' does not link:
#   bc      Mk's own *.y branch is `cc $CFLAGS -o $B y.tab.c -ly'
