# ---- build without installing ---------------------------------------------
# THE ARTEFACTS, one per package, named where the package builds them.  Every
# rule above was `build the thing and copy it to $ROOT' in a single recipe, so
# there was no way to ask for one without the other and `ipnxbuild' installed
# whether it meant to or not.  Each is now two rules -- the artefact, built in
# the source tree and NOT stripped, and the installed file that depends on it
# and is stripped at the destination.  That is the split the design asks for:
# an unstripped strip in /usr/src and a stripped strip in /usr/bin.
#
# So `mk build' is ipnxbuild and `mk world' is ipnxinstall, and the second
# rebuilds nothing because the first already made everything it depends on.
# =U= IS NOT DECORATION.  An unattributed variable is exported into the
# environment of EVERY recipe (var.c's vcopy), and exec charges the environment
# against NCARGS -- include/sys/param.h:10 is (16*1024).  This list is 4,441
# bytes, and adding it plainly pushed the whole environment to 12,201, at which
# point patch's largest seds (5,037 bytes of -e expressions) stopped fitting:
# five `Arg list too long' on the first ipnxbuild ever run.  mk expands $ARTEFACTS
